From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Oliver Sargison <sarol263@student.otago.ac.nz>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 15:28:56 +1300
Subject: [PATCH 18/51] Plutonium: windows held at an agent's size, Take
 control; read_window and act_window

launch_app takes a width and height, and an agent's windows keep the size
it gives them (or the app's own). A window tab shows a held window at that
size, scaled down to fit the panel without stretching, behind a lock that
says the agent is using it (working, while it gives input) and offers
Take control: then the panel sizes the window again. The tab's header
shows the held size, or that an agent is working in a window the user
controls. read_window and act_window read and use a window through the
app's accessibility tree.
